<article class="env-corollary" id="03PM">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03PM">Corollary <span data-tag="03PM">4.5.3.34</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a commutative diagram of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \ar [r]^-{U} \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1 \ar [l] \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_0 \ar [r]^-{V} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}&amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_1, \ar [l] } \]
</div>
<p> where the vertical maps are equivalences of $\infty $-categories. If $U$ and $V$ are isofibrations, then the induced map $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{1} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_0 \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_1$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Corollaries <a data-tag="033L" href="/tag/033L">4.5.3.21</a> and <a data-tag="033T" href="/tag/033T">4.5.3.29</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
